# Application Structure

The main application follows Next.js App Router architecture.

## App Organization

- `(auth)` - Authentication-related routes (sign-in, sign-up, admin)
- `(site)` - Main site routes (explore, history, sightings, timeline, whiteboard)
- `api` - API route handlers

## Key Pages

- [apps/app/src/app/(site)/explore/page.tsx](mdc:ultraterrestrial-resurrection/apps/app/src/app/(site)/explore/page.tsx) - Exploration page
- [apps/app/src/app/(site)/history/page.tsx](mdc:ultraterrestrial-resurrection/apps/app/src/app/(site)/history/page.tsx) - Historical events
- [apps/app/src/app/(site)/sightings/page.tsx](mdc:ultraterrestrial-resurrection/apps/app/src/app/(site)/sightings/page.tsx) - UFO sightings
- [apps/app/src/app/(site)/timeline/page.tsx](mdc:ultraterrestrial-resurrection/apps/app/src/app/(site)/timeline/page.tsx) - Timeline view

## API Routes

- `apps/app/src/app/api/chat` - WIP AI Chat endpoint
- `apps/app/src/app/api/disclosure/chat` - OpenAI Disclosure Assistant Chat API endpoint
- `apps/app/src/app/api/admin` - Admin functionality
- `apps/app/src/app/api/processing` - Data processing endpoints
- `apps/app/src/app/api/disclosure` - Disclosure information endpoints
